<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>(a) Solve <m>-12 \le -4x + 8 \lt 16</m>. Write your answer with the smaller number first.</p><div><fillin characters="5" name="ans1"/> [ &lt; | ≤ | &gt; | ≥ ] <m>x</m> [ &lt; | ≤ | &gt; | ≥ ] <fillin characters="5" name="ans4"/>   </div><p>(b) How many integers satisfy the inequality?</p><div><fillin characters="5" name="ans5"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Do the same thing to all three parts. Subtract <m>{8}</m> from every part: <m>{-20} {\le} {-4x} {\lt} {8}</m>. Divide every part by <m>{-4}</m>, a negative number, so both signs turn round: <m>{5} {\ge} x {\gt} {-2}</m>. Written with the smaller number first, <m>-2 \lt x \le 5</m>. The strict end and the inclusive end have changed places.</p><p>(b) The integers are <m>{\left[ -1 , 0 , 1 , 2 , 3 , 4 , 5 \right]}</m>: there are <m>{7}</m> of them. <m>{-2}</m> is not included (<m>\lt</m>); <m>{5}</m> is included.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>-2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p>&lt;</p></answer>
    <answer><p>≤</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>5</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>7</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>